  "caption": "Quinn thought holding still would be the easiest workout ever. Twenty seconds into a wall sit, the thighs disagreed.\n\nIn an isometric hold, muscles can work very hard even though nothing moves. Because the tendon is loaded without the bounce, holds can suit tendons that are irritable with movement. Results vary, and holds work best as one part of a wider programme.\n\nWhat often helps: pick a simple hold such as a wall sit or wall push, keep breathing rather than straining, combine holds with moving strength work, and get your dose from a physio, especially with heart or blood pressure concerns.\n\nStop and seek help for chest pain, dizziness or unusual breathlessness. A sudden snap at the heel or knee needs same-day attention.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
